out.push(A('_Three sentences, each naming its criterion:_ **"On the mechanism question: _what happens when two of us give different answers_ could not have been answered with reassurance, and the proof is that it was not. On the count with its limitation: _I only see the threads I have answered in_ turns eleven into a floor instead of a claim, which is the strongest thing you could have done with a number you cannot verify. On the smallest fix: one line written by the person who already knows the difference is exactly right, and I would say in the note how long it takes — eight seconds — because the reader is about to ask."**'));
out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('Two counts, and the second is the useful one: not how many said _no questions_, but how many **had** a question and decided not to ask it. It is most of the room, and the reasons are always the same three — I had got what I wanted, it was not my place, and I have always said no. Then Jad\'s arithmetic: three questions on a piece of paper, nearly none used, and the one he nearly did not ask produced ten minutes of four other people\'s thinking and a note he was asked to write. **The question you are least comfortable asking is the one whose answer is _nobody has decided_**, and that answer is the most valuable thing anybody will hand you in an interview.'));
out.push(S('Homework (sample)'));
