out.push(S('I can… (Unit 22)'));
out.push(A('Self-assessment; no answers. The four that matter are the second, the fifth, the sixth and the eighth: asking of any answer whether a stranger could check it, answering _out of what?_ before it is asked, the hard question in two sentences with the unflattering one first, and counting the lines of a document that are doing no work. A class that ticks the cleft and the approximators and not those four has learnt two structures and will give the same two-minute answer in January.'));
out.push(box('Looking ahead to Unit 23', [
  'Units 19 to 22 were about the student\'s own work and their own words. **Unit 23** turns the same scrutiny on everybody else\'s: how a thing that happened becomes a thing that is reported, and what each step does to it.',
  '**23.2 is the cycle to prepare for**: the reporting verbs. _He said · he claimed · he admitted · he denied · he announced · sources say · it is understood._ Each one inserts the writer\'s opinion into a sentence that looks like a fact, and most readers never notice — which is exactly the move the class has spent four units learning to make deliberately about themselves. **23.3** is the passive report — _it is reported that_, _is said to have_ — and what it hides, which is the agent (19.1, now five units old and about to matter again).',
  '**23.7 takes the prediction board down for the last time.** It went up in 14.1, it came down in 18.7 with four of its dates fallen, and in 23.7 the two June dates are read — including Ms Huda\'s own. The board must be in the room; if a class has lost it, reconstruct it from the Unit 18 answer key before the lesson, because the whole of 23.7 is built on reading it.',
  '**Ask the class now for 23.1:** one piece of news they have read or heard this month and **believed**, and one they did **not** believe — and, for each, **the one word in it that decided them.** 23.1 is built on those two words and not on the two stories, and a class that brings the stories without the words has a cycle about the news instead of a cycle about reading.',
], C.lorange, C.orange));

